{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1469259-trinity-continuum-assassins-pre-order","id":1469259,"title":"Trinity Continuum: Assassins Pre-Order","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-11-30T10:03:10-08:00","id":1469259,"title":"Trinity Continuum: Assassins Pre-Order","content":"<b>TC Assassins</b> will release as Pre-Order on <b>DriveThru RPG</b>, not Kickstarter.<br /> Most important info - Pre-Order is to buy here, cost is 19.99$ <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> - <a href=\"https://preview.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/379041/Trinity-Continuum-Assassins-PreOrder\" target=\"_blank\">https://preview.drivethrurpg.com/en/...ssins-PreOrder</a><br /> <br /> The Onyx Path studio will publish a new chapters from the book as part of the Preview every 2 weeks, similar to how they did it on time limited Kickstarters. I do not know what the payment for the Pre-Order will look like, because this is only the second one they are doing, and the first one that I will be watching. I will summarize here how it will be resolved below.<br /> <br /> Here is what we know from <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/terra-surging-monday-meeting-notes/\" target=\"_blank\">this week Monday Meetings Notes</a>...<br /> <br /> <i>On Wednesday, we\u2019re doing something different and offering a <b>Pre-Order</b> page as our sales item of the week. In this case, the Pre-Order for <b>Trinity Continuum: Assassins!</b> We had such success with our Pre-Order for <b>M20 Rich Bastard\u2019s Guide</b>, that we really felt that a book like <b>TC: Assassins</b> would be a fantastic follow-up!<br /> <br /> Here is some official sounding stuff all about that!:<br /> This Wednesday we\u2019ll be setting up the pre-order on <b>DriveThruRPG</b> along with the first couple of chapters of the <b>TC: Assassins</b> manuscript. Then every two weeks or so we\u2019ll be adding more sections of the manuscript, which you\u2019ll get automatically added to your Library on <b>DriveThruRPG</b>.<br /> <br /> Once the PDF has gone through layout we\u2019ll update <b>DriveThruRPG</b> with the <b>Advance PDF</b>. Pre-order customers will get a chance to look at the complete <b>Advance PDF</b> for at least a week before it is released for sale to non pre-order customers.<br /> <br /> We\u2019ll have an errata feedback form available the same as other <b>Advance PDFs</b> we\u2019ve released in the past and we appreciate everyone who sends in those comments.<br /> <br /> Also, from Eddy, here is the description of the chapters:<br /> <br /> While <b>Trinity Continuum Core Rulebook</b> is necessary to play a game of <b>TC: Assassins</b>, this book contains many additions and adjustments to the core ruleset to better shape a chronicle set in the world of shadow. The following chapters detail these additions.<br /> <br /> <b>Chapter One: Stepping into Shadow</b> discusses the hidden world of the Assassins, its history and structure as well as notable figures from the past and present.<br /> <br /> <b>Chapter Two: The Shadow World </b>details the Societies of Shadow. Characters can belong to any of the five introduced in this chapter, but players and Storyguides are welcome to invent their own.<br /> <br /> <b>Chapter Three: Character Creation</b> details the process by which players create their unique Assassins. This chapter contains brand new paths and Edges suitable for playing in the shadow world, as well as all-new Skill Tricks and cutting-edge gear.<br /> <br /> <b>Chapter Four: Systems and Drama</b> explains the rules specific to playing <b>TC: Assassins</b> chronicles. In this chapter Storyguides will also find a collection of deadly antagonists to challenge the players\u2019 characters.<br /> <br /> <b>Chapter Five: Masteries</b> are new, special abilities that only Assassins can access. They grant characters supernatural power over acts of violence, hunting, stalking, and killing.<br /> <br /> <b>Chapter Six: The Killing Art</b> provides advice for Storyguides running Assassins games. It also includes a few sample scenarios, and how to properly pace one\u2019s way through a series of linked assassinations.<br /> <br /> If you haven\u2019t realized it yet, <b>Trinity Continuum: Assassins </b>is a very different look at our Continuum! (Or is it? See art below <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/Denmark_8.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-02-2021, 04:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-01T13:47:38-08:00","id":1469355,"title":"","content":"First few chapters preview is great. I'm considering whether several antagonist groups I'd been tinkering with should in fact be Anathema Assassins. I made up the &quot;Chakravarti&quot; to specifically combine the Pulp villain staples of Nazis and Thuggee by having them be Hinduism-appropriating Aryanists who believe cycles of destruction are necessary to serve social darwinism and renew the &quot;natural order&quot;.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Amarenth Concern&quot; are dedicated to preventing world threatening scientific breakthroughs by staying one step head with regard to technological potential and consequences and taking out the researchers they need to - but even as that agenda alone served to make them Anathema since many of their targets are in Daylight, they've also been corrupted by taking contracts to protect certain business interests from destabilizing technological threats (such as from the fossil fuel industry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-01T16:25:56-08:00","id":1469370,"title":"","content":"So, if Assassins is not going to be Kickstarted, will the physical book have the same format as the Kickstarter hardcovers of the other games so far?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-01T21:24:06-08:00","id":1469380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1469259-trinity-continuum-assassins-pre-order?p=1469370#post1469370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, if Assassins is not going to be Kickstarted, will the physical book have the same format as the Kickstarter hardcovers of the other games so far?</div> </div> </div> </div>To date, three TC books (TC core, \u00c6on, Aberrant) have been Kickstarted. There have been an additional eleven supplements, four of which have been available in hardcover.<br /> <br /> They've <i>all </i>had the same basic format. There's no reason why Assassins would be an exception to that, and we're not planning on changing that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-02T00:40:29-08:00","id":1469386,"title":"","content":"I liked the links that the Core book had to Shadow. The Aeon / Jacobin links specifically provide food for thought.<br /> It will be interesting to see if they will come out with a source book detailing Assassins thru the ages. I would love to see how the Society's deal with the Psion Orders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27184-darrendalca","name":"DarrenDalca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27184_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-02T01:08:53-08:00","id":1469387,"title":"","content":"Most important info - Pre-Order is to buy here <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> - <a href=\"https://preview.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/379041/Trinity-Continuum-Assassins-PreOrder\" target=\"_blank\">https://preview.drivethrurpg.com/en/...ssins-PreOrder</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-02-2021, 04:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-02T11:51:24-08:00","id":1469411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarrenDalca</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1469259-trinity-continuum-assassins-pre-order?p=1469386#post1469386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked the links that the Core book had to Shadow. The Aeon / Jacobin links specifically provide food for thought.<br /> It will be interesting to see if they will come out with a source book detailing Assassins thru the ages. I would love to see how the Society's deal with the Psion Orders.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Directive on the Ministry of Noetic Affairs, Entire Preliminary Statement:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=979\" data-tempid=\"temp_979_1638474658276_152\" /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-02T13:01:56-08:00","id":1469415,"title":"","content":"Well, I pre-ordered this. I wonder if this proves to be successful, they could do a supplement like Assassins in other eras. I would be curious as to what assassins would look like specifically in the Anima-era (for things like Shadowrun-type knockoffs), Aberrant (would be interesting and to see what happens if a Nova enters the Shadows), Aeon - (alien assassin societies, space, psions and how Noetics works with the Shadow, and just future tech etc.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26453,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26453-worldsaverinc","user":"worldsaverinc","date":". 12-02-2021, 04:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26453-worldsaverinc","name":"worldsaverinc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-02T14:48:27-08:00","id":1469418,"title":"","content":"1. It\u2019s cool to see to see several foes of Core Allegiances show up. Baphomet (foe of Archangel) and the Society of Minos (foe of the Theseus Club) specifically.<br /> <br /> 2. Theseus Assassins would be an interesting topic to address/include at the game table!<br /> <br /> 3. It really seems like La Revolte Eclatante hasn\u2019t shown up since the core because someone decided \u201cNo wait, scratch that, let\u2019s make them Assassins\u201d, hence the Haiti based Daughters of the Jacobins.<br /> <br /> 4. The Heavenly Immortal Corps reinforces my desire to see a Wuxia genre supplement/setting for TC (including examining and deconstructing Yellow Peril tropes and Orientalism in drawing in Wuxia in Adventure! Aether or Aberrant)!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-03T10:59:33-08:00","id":1469509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>worldsaverinc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1469259-trinity-continuum-assassins-pre-order?p=1469415#post1469415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I pre-ordered this. I wonder if this proves to be successful, they could do a supplement like Assassins in other eras.</div> </div> </div> </div>This would indeed be awesome! In fact, I think the concept of &quot;Assassins&quot; would work in just about any era of Trinity. Given, that &quot;Assassins&quot; could be called &quot;The Assassination Bureau - the RPG&quot;, even Adventure! and Aether could work just splendid! <br /> <br /> Speaking of &quot;The Assassination Bureau&quot; - might either equipment or masteries contain exploding Blutwurst? And, more important, would assassination by said Blutwurst be a violation of the Code? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24955-waldi","name":"Waldi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-03T19:07:55-08:00","id":1469548,"title":"","content":"So far I'm loving the material made available via pre-order--but then, this entire line has been batting 1000 for me with regard to the writing, and I love the spy/assassin/thriller genre besides (so it would need to have really stunk for this to not have been a 'love at first sight' situation.) Having said that, I'm hoping there was some attempt to systematized different styles of combat/fighting and killing such that there's fun distinctions; highly stylized methods of dispatching folks is sort of a trope of the genre. Obviously the way Nicholai Hel kills people (with his &quot;naked/kill&quot; style,) is vastly different from the way John Wick (or any one of a number of the killers in the John Wick movies,) does it. I'm not expecting anything revolutionary, but I'm excited to see the attempt (if any).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-03T21:16:34-08:00","id":1469553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1469259-trinity-continuum-assassins-pre-order?p=1469418#post1469418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. It\u2019s cool to see to see several foes of Core Allegiances show up. Baphomet (foe of Archangel) and the Society of Minos (foe of the Theseus Club) specifically.<br /> <br /> 2. Theseus Assassins would be an interesting topic to address/include at the game table!<br /> <br /> 3. It really seems like La Revolte Eclatante hasn\u2019t shown up since the core because someone decided \u201cNo wait, scratch that, let\u2019s make them Assassins\u201d, hence the Haiti based Daughters of the Jacobins.<br /> <br /> 4. The Heavenly Immortal Corps reinforces my desire to see a Wuxia genre supplement/setting for TC (including examining and deconstructing Yellow Peril tropes and Orientalism in drawing in Wuxia in Adventure! Aether or Aberrant)!</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m gonna make La Revolte Eclatante a Daylight Allegiance of social justice activists allied with the Daughters of the Jacobins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-03T23:10:07-08:00","id":1469559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>worldsaverinc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1469259-trinity-continuum-assassins-pre-order?p=1469415#post1469415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I pre-ordered this. I wonder if this proves to be successful, they could do a supplement like Assassins in other eras. I would be curious as to what assassins would look like specifically in the Anima-era (for things like Shadowrun-type knockoffs), Aberrant (would be interesting and to see what happens if a Nova enters the Shadows), Aeon - (alien assassin societies, space, psions and how Noetics works with the Shadow, and just future tech etc.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I cant find it, but somewhere in the forum Ian Watson (or Bunyip I don't remember) says something about how Shadow is a subtle effect and those with Inspiration aren't really affected by the perception filter that Assassin buildings get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27184-darrendalca","name":"DarrenDalca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27184_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-06T03:15:15-08:00","id":1469713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1469259-trinity-continuum-assassins-pre-order?p=1469553#post1469553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019m gonna make La Revolte Eclatante a Daylight Allegiance of social justice activists allied with the Daughters of the Jacobins.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds good - especially since similar things would also be very logical with other Allegiances. With some Allegiances in other eras, the whole thing is even clearer. I would be very surprised, for example, if De Vries in Aberrant or Norca un Aeon had no connections to the shadow.<br /> <br /> My take on assassins in the Aberrant era would be that the whole basic situation is still comparatively similar to that in the present - with two differences: &quot;The Signal&quot; specialises more and more in eliminating novas that are dangerous for Baseline people - they mutate into &quot;The Boys&quot;, so to speak. In the process, they have entered into alliances of convenience with the Directive on more than one occasion.<br /> The Swarm, on the other hand, has dropped to the status of a minor society thanks to internal disputes and financial problems. In exchange, De Vries is now part of the Council.<br /> <br /> In Aeon, I would find it quite interesting if an Assassin society was a secret militant arm of ISRA. This highly dangerous and surprisingly fanatical group uses precognition to determine what kind of people could endanger humanity in the future and then has them eliminated before they can do any harm.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24955-waldi","name":"Waldi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-06T03:40:49-08:00","id":1469714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarrenDalca</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1469259-trinity-continuum-assassins-pre-order?p=1469559#post1469559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I cant find it, but somewhere in the forum Ian Watson (or Bunyip I don't remember) says something about how Shadow is a subtle effect and those with Inspiration aren't really affected by the perception filter that Assassin buildings get.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m guessing Ian (or maybe Neall) - I haven\u2019t worked on Assassin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-10T08:47:03-08:00","id":1470139,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">i'm just cynical about the whole thing going this preorder route instead of kickstarter. with ks they give you the previews over the course of the KS to keep you till the end where they get your money. why are they doing that here? the text is written they already have our money why make us wait for the staggered previews and two weeks between installments. hell KS gets the previews weekly. and if the text isn't written then why the rush/ finish the writing and then do the KS.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">no stretch goals for bonus for being an early backer, no premium hardback, previews stretched over two months and they already got my cash. Yeah this is the new model i'm sure, and i'm not happy about it.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">just to clarify I am not saying this supplement or the game is at fault or even the writers. but OP management, seriously we have to work for our money too and up to this book you usually make a good value for supporting you early, but this just stinks of a cash grab. I hope i am wrong. </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25501-nina_blain","name":"nina_blain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-10T09:11:30-08:00","id":1470142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nina_blain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1469259-trinity-continuum-assassins-pre-order?p=1470139#post1470139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">i'm just cynical about the whole thing going this preorder route instead of kickstarter. with ks they give you the previews over the course of the KS to keep you till the end where they get your money. why are they doing that here? the text is written they already have our money why make us wait for the staggered previews and two weeks between installments. hell KS gets the previews weekly. and if the text isn't written then why the rush/ finish the writing and then do the KS.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">no stretch goals for bonus for being an early backer, no premium hardback, previews stretched over two months and they already got my cash. Yeah this is the new model i'm sure, and i'm not happy about it.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">just to clarify I am not saying this supplement or the game is at fault or even the writers. but OP management, seriously we have to work for our money too and up to this book you usually make a good value for supporting you early, but this just stinks of a cash grab. I hope i am wrong. </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think assuming they're going to make a significantly greater profit with this model is pretty detached from the reality of sales in this industry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 12-10-2021, 12:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-10T09:28:06-08:00","id":1470145,"title":"","content":"I'm curious what they <i>do</i> expect to get out of a gradual release, instead of just providing the full manuscript right away. I mean, if it works for them, great! But I'm just not seeing what the benefit is to Onyx Path, compared to the way RBGTM was handled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-10T11:19:26-08:00","id":1470153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1469259-trinity-continuum-assassins-pre-order?p=1470145#post1470145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious what they <i>do</i> expect to get out of a gradual release, instead of just providing the full manuscript right away. I mean, if it works for them, great! But I'm just not seeing what the benefit is to Onyx Path, compared to the way RBGTM was handled.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not having to run multiple Kickstarters at once.<br /> <br /> The full preview not being there at once is a bit weird, but the obvious benefit is &quot;we only have so many hours in a day and one community manager.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-10T11:26:15-08:00","id":1470154,"title":"","content":"And Kickstarter is making noise about wanting creators to have shipped their latest Kickstarter before starting another. Also, if they aren't going to do a traditional print run, there's no reason to use Kickstarter. There isn't the initial monetary layout needed for PDF and PoD. Finally, I'm assuming the pre-order drip builds more hype than just releasing a book. I prefer this to getting a blurb about Assassins on the Monday Meeting Notes every week for a month or two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-10T12:41:43-08:00","id":1470160,"title":"","content":"The reason we're doing a gradual manuscript release for Assassins is exactly the same reason we do it on Kickstarter: because we get more targeted discussion that way.<br /> <br /> When we throw the whole manuscript at people, the discussions are very general or might focus in on one or two things that people liked overall.<br /> <br /> If we release the manuscript in sections, then people discuss what's in those sections and have a chance to digest them before the next manuscript section is released.<br /> <br /> It's better discussion on forums like here or Discord, and it provides a better result when the time comes for submitting playtest feedback or errata.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-10T19:51:32-08:00","id":1470181,"title":"","content":"I...did not think about that part. But it does make sense that releasing the chapter on, say, Masteries, would mean the conversation of the day/week/what have you is only about the Masteries and any feedback would help you guys perfect them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T10:29:48-08:00","id":1470450,"title":"","content":"I really enjoyed the Assassins' factions. The Society of Leonidas and the Daughters of the Jacobins seem to have a relationship like the Templars and Assassins in Assassin's Creed, whose transhistorical plotline has always reminded me of the Trinity Continuum. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">There's an implication in Anima that there exists technology like the Animus machine, too!</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"u