 to somehow incorporate a device that at least resembles the Animus from Assassin's Creed. There might not be a genetic memory, but there are heaps of strange PSI powers. Possibly a Trinity version of the Animus could simply be based on Noetics. Perhaps the machine will allow the user to relive past events via biotechnically enhanced clairsentience. This fits more to AEON than to Continuum, but there is always something... </div></div> </div> </div> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24955-waldi","name":"Waldi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T12:39:21-08:00","id":1470463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Waldi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1469259-trinity-continuum-assassins-pre-order?p=1470461#post1470461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Yeah, the &quot;genetic memory&quot; thing wouldn't really fit into the Trinity Continuum. However, off the top of my head, I would have a few ideas on how to somehow incorporate a device that at least resembles the Animus from Assassin's Creed. There might not be a genetic memory, but there are heaps of strange PSI powers. Possibly a Trinity version of the Animus could simply be based on Noetics. Perhaps the machine will allow the user to relive past events via biotechnically enhanced clairsentience. This fits more to AEON than to Continuum, but there is always something... </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah a Noetic device that incorporates Telepathy and Clairsentience to experience the lives of people in the past would make sense!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T12:41:48-08:00","id":1470464,"title":"","content":"Not the case for anima, but if you have something similar to Noetic Connection or Quantum Attunement but applied to Flux, in the form of a cross time connection to your ancestry, that is what Assassins Creed machine would use to fit the concept. It would feels a lot like genetic memory, but not really in your genes, but in your genealogy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-15T20:06:53-08:00","id":1470579,"title":"","content":"Okay; so from the description of Masteries, it looks kind of like Assassins are a \u201cstep up\u201d from Talents, in that their Masteries actually let them do impossible things, like bending bullet trajectories. On the other hand, that's why we have the Daylight/Twilight/Shadow divide: so that the impossible things that Assassins can do don't end up making the news and becoming public knowledge. <br /> <br /> Also, I really like the Flashbacks take on Dramatic Editing. I forget the name of the Mega-Edge in TC:Ab that gives Mega-Intelligent Novas access to DE; but it had to do with always being prepared; and I would explicitly \u201climit\u201d it to Flashbacks \u2014 not that that's much of a limitation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-16T03:47:03-08:00","id":1470602,"title":"","content":"Flux in the hand of assassins is a real tool and they know they are using it, not like a talent. That is something very interesting to explore.<br /> <br /> Now, can a Talent learn a Mastery? Or a Assassin learn a Gift? Because many of the things Black Widow and Hawk Eye do, for example, are very much a mix between gifts and masteries.<br /> <br /> Batman, for example, works more like an Assassin, with a dual life (day light and twilight mainly, but some shadow) and lots of masteries to hunt people and put them down, he even have some ninja training (by some I mean a lot), yet he doesn\u2019t kill people and he invents some super-tech (not a remarkable super inventor, but he does).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-16T18:06:38-08:00","id":1470677,"title":"","content":"Oh: something else from the manuscript that I liked. The flashback rules let you choose whether to pay for a flashback with inspiration or momentum. It costs twice as much momentum as inspiration; but the option is there. I very much like this as a general rule for dramatic editing. I especially like it in that since momentum is a currency that everyone has access to, it would be a small step to make dramatic editing available to everyone; talents and assassins are merely better at it. (I would also say that as long as momentum is a pooled resource, dramatic editing via momentum should require groupwide collaboration.)<br /> <br /> I would also have no problem with making assassins available in a Nova chronicle, <i>without</i> the cover of Shadow. I also feel that Masteries need not be restricted to assassins \u2014 that is, there's a lot of conceptual space available for \u201cpeople with Masteries\u201d that doesn't fit the paradigm of assassination. I personally have no problem with Assassins also having Gifts alongside their Masteries; but I personally view this supplement more as a starting point, and would have no problem with there also being Assassin-like characters (in the sense that they have Masteries) who have nothing to do with hunting and killing. For the core book's era, they too would operate on a wainscot world similar to the Shadow; but the character of that world would likely be different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 12-18-2021, 06:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-19T15:19:42-08:00","id":1470888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1469259-trinity-continuum-assassins-pre-order?p=1470579#post1470579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay; so from the description of Masteries, it looks kind of like Assassins are a \u201cstep up\u201d from Talents, in that their Masteries actually let them do impossible things, like bending bullet trajectories. On the other hand, that's why we have the Daylight/Twilight/Shadow divide: so that the impossible things that Assassins can do don't end up making the news and becoming public knowledge.<br /> <br /> Also, I really like the Flashbacks take on Dramatic Editing. I forget the name of the Mega-Edge in TC:Ab that gives Mega-Intelligent Novas access to DE; but it had to do with always being prepared; and I would explicitly \u201climit\u201d it to Flashbacks \u2014 not that that's much of a limitation.</div> </div> </div> </div>they are more powerful than Talents AT WHAT THEY DO, but Masteries are a lot more thematically focused than Gifts, so I think there\u2019s a definite trade-off in play rather than Assassins being objectively a step up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-21T03:56:22-08:00","id":1470997,"title":"","content":"Just asking:<br /> <br /> Of course Assassins, like Continuum, is set in the present. But let's just assume that Assassins would be slightly shifted historically: In which era would it fit best?<br /> <br /> When I think about it, I always get stuck in the 1960s. The Cold War, Mafia disputes, social unrest, etc. certainly provide many opportunities for skilful assassination. Moreover, the historical epoch makes the Society of Leonidas' mission to retrieve stolen artefacts from Nazis much more fun. In the 1960s, quite a few of the Nazis in question may still be alive and active. In contrast to today, where the few remaining Nazi war criminals are now between 90 and 100 years old and suddenly shouting &quot;Boo!&quot; loudly is enough for a successful assassination.<br /> <br /> I think the only thing that would have to be changed would be the origin story of &quot;The Swarm&quot;. But then the group was created in the Japanese post-war turmoil and not in the Japanese economic crisis turmoil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24955-waldi","name":"Waldi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-21T04:50:49-08:00","id":1471004,"title":"","content":"I personally would go for a Victorian age assassins or maybe a 1930s, to get the Noir feeling both periods may have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-03T05:31:37-08:00","id":1471728,"title":"","content":"Revision 3 PDF preview, a 173 page document, is 'final' version of preview? No new PDF revisions will be on Pre-Order?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-03T06:36:53-08:00","id":1471729,"title":"","content":"This is the full length of the current manuscript. The final manuscript will be longer if for no other reason than added art and formatting. I wouldn\u2019t be surprised if preorderers got a preview of the final manuscript before it\u2019s release during an errata phase, but I ha